{"shortDescription":"The American Hospital Association has once again filed a lawsuit to halt a new pilot that tests a revised rebate model for the 340B Drug Pricing Program, a federal benefits program for underinsured and low-income Americans.The AHA, the Maine Hospital Association, and four safety-net hospitals filed…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The American Hospital Association has once again filed a lawsuit to halt a new pilot that tests a revised rebate model for the 340B Drug Pricing Program, a federal benefits program for underinsured and low-income Americans."]},{"type":"p","children":["The AHA, the Maine Hospital Association, and four safety-net hospitals filed the suit on Thursday, naming the Health and Human Services Department and the Health Resources and Services Administration, the HHS unit overseeing the program, among its defendants."]},{"type":"p","children":["The lawsuit was filed in a federal court in Maine days after the HRSA announced the pilot, which allows 10 pharmaceutical manufacturers to offer after-the-fact rebates instead of upfront discounts on 21 drugs ",{"type":"url","params":{"url":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4650023-abbvie-among-participants-new-340b-rebate-pilot?utm_source=tradingview\u0026utm_medium=referral\u0026feed_item_type=news","linkText":"purchased under the program."}}]},{"type":"p","children":["The Trump administration’s first 340B rebate pilot, which applied to only 10 medicines, was blocked by a federal judge in December following a lawsuit from the AHA and several hospital systems. The HHS formally withdrew the plan in January after losing on appeal."]},{"type":"p","children":["The latest complaint seeks a temporary and permanent block on the program, which is set to take effect on Jan. 1 with the participation of drugmakers including AbbVie ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:ABBV","text":"NYSE:ABBV"}},", Amgen ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:AMGN","text":"NASDAQ:AMGN"}},", Astellas ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"OTC:ALPMF","text":"OTC:ALPMF"}},", AstraZeneca ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:AZN","text":"NYSE:AZN"}},", Bristol Myers ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:BMY","text":"NYSE:BMY"}},", GSK ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:GSK","text":"NYSE:GSK"}},", Merck ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:MRK","text":"NYSE:MRK"}},", Pfizer ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:PFE","text":"NYSE:PFE"}},", and Teva ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:TEVA","text":"NYSE:TEVA"}},"."]},{"type":"p","children":["It makes arguments similar to the first, noting that the pilot doesn’t account for substantial costs the providers will have to incur by purchasing the drugs at market prices and then applying for rebates."]},{"type":"p","children":["Listed hospital systems: HCA Healthcare ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:HCA","text":"NYSE:HCA"}},", Community Health Systems ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:CYH","text":"NYSE:CYH"}},", Surgery Partners ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:SGRY","text":"NASDAQ:SGRY"}},", Tenet Healthcare ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:THC","text":"NYSE:THC"}},", Universal Health Services ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:UHS","text":"NYSE:UHS"}},", Select Medical Holdings (SEM), Acadia Healthcare ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:ACHC","text":"NASDAQ:ACHC"}},", LifeStance Health Group ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:LFST","text":"NASDAQ:LFST"}},{"type":"disclaimer","children":["Content provided by Seeking Alpha is intended for information purposes only, and that Seeking Alpha does not offer any personalist investment advice and is not a licensed securities dealer, broker, US investment adviser or investment bank."]}]}]},"language":"en","tags":[{"title":"Seeking Alpha","args":[{"id":"provider","value":"seekingalpha"}]},{"title":"US stocks","args":[{"id":"category","va